<p>The <span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody"><a href="https://internationalsocietymoralpsychology.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">International Society for Moral Psychology</a> (ISMP) is a new association that aims to be an &#8220;</span>interdisciplinary and international home for moral psychology, aimed at fostering deeper engagement across traditions, methodologies, and cultural contexts.&#8221;<span id="more-57122"></span></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-57123 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/international-society-moral-psychology.png" alt="" width="578" height="330" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/international-society-moral-psychology.png 700w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/international-society-moral-psychology-300x171.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/international-society-moral-psychology-400x229.png 400w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 578px) 100vw, 578px" /></p>
<p>An announcement from the association states that ISMP is &#8220;focused on two initiatives: an annual conference, and a mentoring program for graduate students, postdocs, and early-career scholars with interests in moral psychology from anywhere in the world.&#8221; The first conference will be at Cornell University in September.</p>
<p>Additionally, at the moment you can join the organization at no cost:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Thanks to a generous grant from Templeton World Charities Foundation, membership in ISMP is free for a limited time. We cordially invite you, and your students and colleagues to<strong> <a href="https://internationalsocietymoralpsychology.com/join-ismp/">join ISMP</a></strong>. </em></p>
<p>The inaugural president of ISMP is <a href="https://www.valerietiberius.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Valerie Tiberius</a> (University of Minnesota) and its vice-president is <a href="https://psychology.cornell.edu/laura-niemi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Laura Niemi</a> (Cornell), who with  <a href="https://philosophy.cornell.edu/john-m-doris" target="_blank" rel="noopener">John Doris</a> (Cornell), is also co-project director.</p>
<p>You learn more about the organization <a href="https://internationalsocietymoralpsychology.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/04/13/new-international-society-for-moral-psychology/">New: International Society for Moral Psychology</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>